        "firmware_body": {
          "error": "A version is required (e.g. 1.1.0)"
        }
      },
      "findings": [
        "POST /api/firmware is not authorization-gated. The probe reached the handler's input validation (HTTP 400, {'error': 'A version is required (e.g. 1.1.0)'}) rather than an authz check, and in source the route is registered ABOVE the `/admin` block while publishFirmware() never calls isAdmin() \u2014 so any authenticated account can publish a fleet-wide OTA image. (This run's caller IS an admin, so the 403 was not expected for them; the defect is proven by the missing gate in code plus the handler being reached. Confirming it empirically needs a second, non-admin account.)"
      ]
