      },
      "findings": [
        "deleting the session did NOT delete the recording it produced. deleteSession() removes the sate_device_sessions row and its object in the device-sessions bucket, but the derived `recordings` row (e325c7c6-33ef-4bd0-99c1-bb28d72dfd40) and its copy of the audio in the recordings bucket (bc324864-51a6-4328-be68-d7b0dadaabce/1788749956355_device_SATE-443EAC_s92.wav) both survive. The take still appears in the web app and the audio is still downloadable, so 'delete' does not delete the clinical data \u2014 the opposite of what a retention/erasure request needs.",
        "no audit-trail table is reachable (sate_audit_log=404, audit_log=404, sate_events=404, session_audit=404) \u2014 deletions and retries leave no auditable record, which SEC-007 and BE-012 both require."
      ]
