        "b": 200,
        "final_text": "writer B",
        "malformed": 400
      },
      "findings": [
        "writer B's save (HTTP 200) silently overwrote writer A's \u2014 final text is 'writer B'. Saves go straight to PostgREST with no version check, no If-Match/ETag and no updated_at precondition, so two clinicians editing the same transcript lose one set of edits with no warning and no way to recover it (there is no server-side history to recover from)."
